Z||000000||William Federle||11-03-1999||05:19 PM||||Does anyone know what the cold idle speed<BR>should be for a 1984 4 cyl std shift fiero?<BR>I don't think I have a vacuum leak. I've<BR>just put on a new TPS and noticed very<BR>improved drivability when cold - but the idle<BR>when I first start the engine at approx. 32<BR>deg F is 3000 RPM. It slows to about 2500 after about 20 seconds. I've got the thermac<BR>air cleaner connected to the outlet on the<BR>muffler and I've seen it working. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eddie||11-03-1999||06:02 PM||||MY wifes z34 did the same thing at start up it was not the TPS it was the IAC valve for your car its abuot $60.00 but its worth it 3000 rpms at start up is very high my fiero  is a 1987 it starts up at 1800 rpms .||||reg||6
