Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||11-04-1999||08:01 AM||||Where is the vacuum sensor on a V6?  I was revving up a little of 2K rpms and yesterday I was at a stop light after starting the car and was revving at 2K off and on until I got home and reset the ECM.  Now my hesitation is worse since the resetting and seems to happen off and on even when it warms up.<P>Last night I replaced my TPS and it didn't work, so I am going to take it back.||||reg||1
Z||000005||William Federle||11-04-1999||08:21 AM||||On my 4 cyl. 1984 fiero the vacuum sensor is<BR>located on the R.H. side of the air cleaner - I think. I believe its a flat plastic assem. about 3" long with a 3 pin connector<BR>and a vacuum hose that connects to the throttle body. So maybe on the V6 it is a<BR>similar device.||||reg||1
