Z||000012||William Federle||11-06-1999||06:10 PM||||Well, I replaced the manifold pressure sensor<BR>and two vacuum hoses that had flat spots in<BR>them (as if they had gotten too hot when<BR>laying on something) but the idle is still<BR>3000 for about 20 sec. and then slows down<BR>to 2500 or 2000 depending on the temp. I heard that an error code is set if the ECM<BR>is unable to maintain an RPM within 50 RPM<BR>so that is why didn't start with the IAC<BR>valve. I guess that's next unless someone<BR>has another idea (hopefully less expensive).<BR>||||reg||1
