Z||000015||DXR_DAD||11-07-1999||12:11 AM||||I just got my second fiero, a 87 coupe. William and jhar I seem to be having somewhat of the same problems with mine, (See It's a boy post) I have not worked on the 4cyl DIS. fieros at all. I could also use all the help I can get. That 500rpm has got me!!||||reg||5
Z||000016||Dan||11-07-1999||09:03 AM|||| On a high idle like that, check your throttle body carburator.I had one that had the butterfly brass bushings worn and it gave the same problems.On the ecm,it constantly updates itself and reacts accordingly as long as the inputs are within parameters.Reseting it only reloads the default values from the pprom,and normally after that a short drive should realign the computer.As mentioned earlier it also clears the codes.||||reg||1
Z||000017||theogre||11-07-1999||12:00 PM||||On the DIS motors make sure the spark plugs & wires are good. otherwise there's notthing to do to them.<P>check the trottle shaft for wear. If it's worn enough then the idle stop screw may need a tweek. if it's real worn then you may need to find another TBI unit.<P>Seems when first started cold most of these motors idle high. they should settle down fairly quickly. <P>On the 87+ 4 cyls, especially w/ automatic tranny, check out the trunk wall and make sure the air cleaner hasn't been hitting it. If it has you could have scragged the gasket at the base of the TBI. Check the earlier years too. if the dog bone is bad you could have this problem. A leaking TBI base gasket may not be obvious. If there is evidence the air cleanner hit the trunk wall replace the gasket, and the dog bone. on the 87 w/ automatic push the motor all the way forward when you tighten the dog bone.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fierospeeder||11-07-1999||08:01 PM||||I have the same prob. with my 84 2.5L automatic flame thrower forgot my rods are good.  But, when it would be really cold outside, i would start the car up, and it would rev up to 2000-2500.  After a few minutes you see the rpms dropping. I know the throttle isn't stuck, its just computer controlled which is messing it up.  Is there something like the air cleaner that has a spring and when it gets a certain temp.  vacuum is used to move a compenant?  ||||reg||1
